WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.240 line:87%
In my short life
I've had the occasion to learn

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:14.000 line:1%
and teach through various methods
in different countries.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.360 line:94%
What I like about theatre is that

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:23.600 line:87%
it can turn reality into magic
and magic into reality.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.240 line:87%
The actresses and actors of our theatre
are very different,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.040 line:87%
each of them comes from a unique
background.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.240 line:87%
They have one thing in common
though —

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.560 line:94%
they are homeless or disabled,

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.520 line:87%
people with serious
mental health issues.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.840 line:87%
During the ten years that we have been
doing theatre with the homeless,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:01:00.040 line:87%
we have noticed that the theatre grants
them a feeling of safety.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:05.400 line:87%
There is the space where they can do,
say, show things,

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:11.360 line:87%
that they would never be able to show
in everyday life,

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.520 line:94%
because there wouldn't be room for it.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.720 line:87%
Theatre can help people to develop
relationships.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.400 line:87%
The ability to travel outside
my home country,

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.320 line:94%
to meet and work with others,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:37.560 line:87%
was for me and our theatre a powerful
driving force over the past years.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.760 line:94%
Without an effective teaching

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:46.000 line:87%
and practice-sharing tool
such as Erasmus+,

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.480 line:87%
a majority of these things
would never happen.

